.TH AIO_READ 3 "2026-07-03" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
aio_read \- asynchronous read
.SH LIBRARY
Realtime library (librt, \-lrt)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <aio.h>
.PP
.BI "int aio_read(struct aiocb *" aiocbp );
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR aio_read ()
queues an asynchronous read request described by
.RB * aiocbp
and returns immediately.  The operation reads
.I aio_nbytes
bytes from the file descriptor
.I aio_fildes
starting at offset
.I aio_offset
into the buffer
.IR aio_buf .
.PP
The control block is:
.PP
.nf
struct aiocb {
    int             aio_fildes;    /* file descriptor */
    off_t           aio_offset;    /* file offset */
    volatile void  *aio_buf;       /* buffer */
    size_t          aio_nbytes;    /* transfer length */
    int             aio_reqprio;   /* request priority (advisory) */
    struct sigevent aio_sigevent;  /* completion notification */
    int             aio_lio_opcode;/* used by lio_listio() */
};
.fi
.PP
When the operation completes, notification is delivered as described by
.IR aio_sigevent :
.B SIGEV_NONE
(none),
.B SIGEV_SIGNAL
(a signal), or
.B SIGEV_THREAD
(a function call in a new thread).  Progress and results are retrieved with
.BR aio_error (3)
and
.BR aio_return (3);
completion may be awaited with
.BR aio_suspend (3).
.PP
On Substrate, asynchronous I/O is implemented by a userspace worker-thread
pool (in librt) that performs the underlying
.BR pread (2);
the calling thread is never blocked by
.BR aio_read ().
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success 0 is returned (the request was queued).  On error \-1 is returned
and
.I errno
is set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EAGAIN
Insufficient resources to queue the request, or the number of outstanding
asynchronous I/O operations would exceed
.BR {AIO_MAX} ,
the limit reported by
.BR sysconf (_SC_AIO_MAX).
An operation is outstanding from submission until its status is retrieved
with
.BR aio_return (3).
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I aiocbp
is NULL, or
.I aio_reqprio
or
.I aio_offset
is negative.  When prioritized I/O is supported
.RB ( sysconf (_SC_PRIORITIZED_IO)),
a lower
.I aio_reqprio
is a higher priority and its request is serviced first.
.PP
Errors from the underlying
.BR pread (2)
are reported asynchronously and retrieved with
.BR aio_error (3).
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
char buf[512];
struct aiocb cb = { 0 };
cb.aio_fildes = fd;
cb.aio_buf    = buf;
cb.aio_nbytes = sizeof(buf);
cb.aio_sigevent.sigev_notify = SIGEV_NONE;
aio_read(&cb);
const struct aiocb *l[1] = { &cb };
aio_suspend(l, 1, NULL);
ssize_t n = aio_return(&cb);
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aio_write (3),
.BR aio_suspend (3),
.BR aio_error (3),
.BR aio_return (3)
